## WEBHOOKS

### Configure Webhook

**Endpoint:** `POST /webhooks`

**Request:**
```json
{
  \"url\": \"https://your-domain.com/pxn-webhook\",
  \"events\": [
    \"mandate.generated\",
    \"proof.verified\",
    \"coherence.low_threshold\",
    \"mzs.locked\",
    \"mzs.unlocked\",
    \"drift.detected\",
    \"grace_event.logged\"
  ],
  \"secret\": \"whsec_your_secret_key\"
}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  \"webhookId\": \"wh_123abc\",
  \"url\": \"https://your-domain.com/pxn-webhook\",
  \"events\": [ ... ],
  \"status\": \"active\",
  \"createdAt\": \"2025-12-01T16:30:00Z\"
}
```

### Webhook Payload Example

**Event:** `mandate.generated`

```json
{
  \"event\": \"mandate.generated\",
  \"timestamp\": \"2025-12-01T09:00:00Z\",
  \"data\": {
    \"mandateId\": \"cam_456def\",
    \"operatorId\": \"op_123\",
    \"summary\": \"Contact one stakeholder and commit to listening\",
    \"loveCoefficient\": 0.9456,
    \"mzsLocked\": false,
    \"dueBy\": \"2025-12-01T23:59:59Z\"
  },
  \"signature\": \"sha256=...\"
}
```

### Webhook Signature Verification

Webhooks are signed using HMAC-SHA256 with your webhook secret.

```python
import hmac
import hashlib

def verify_webhook(payload, signature, secret):
    expected = hmac.new(
        secret.encode(),
        payload.encode(),
        hashlib.sha256
    ).hexdigest()
    return hmac.compare_digest(f\"sha256={expected}\", signature)
```

